@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] firmware-image-offline-assembly
Windows guest images MUST be assembled from a hash-pinned installation ISO
recorded in iso.json, the pinned nixpkgs virtio-win driver tree and the
source-built CloudHv firmware, inside a KVM-enabled Nix sandbox whose guest
network is restricted. Core guest agents come only from the source-built
`lyraWindows` and `terminaldWindows` derivations, and the optional candidate
editor broker only from the source-built `windowsEditorBroker`; winget and every
winget package (Git among them) only from winget.json, fetched by Nix against
the recorded SHA-256 digests. The managed GitHub CLI and LFS replacements MUST
be source-built from the separate hash-pinned `guest/github` derivations and
staged offline before setup. No build step may fetch anything at build time;
the installation guest's only reachable endpoint is the guestfwd file server
serving exactly the staged installers, and the installation MUST bind
modern-only virtio-pci devices (ADR-0169, ADR-0171, ADR-0173).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] windows-serial-console
A Windows guest image MUST boot headless with Emergency Management Services on
COM1 at 115200 baud (boot manager, loader and SAC), MUST NOT autologon (the
build's single interactive logon, AutoLogon LogonCount 1 for the winget step of
ADR-0173, MUST leave no AutoAdminLogon, DefaultPassword or AutoLogonCount
behind, and the image is refused without OVERALLS-AUTOLOGON-CLEARED), and MUST
carry only the documented bootstrap Administrator credential until the roster
agent retires it: on a `windows-v1` guest the agent MUST give the Administrator
a random unrecorded password and disable it as soon as a roster account is
active (ADR-0171), after which the SAC prompt offers no usable login. On the
agentless image the SAC login shell on serial remains an explicit difference
from the Linux no-serial-login-shell contract and MUST stay recorded as a
security gap while it exists.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] windows-image-identity-separate
Ordinary Windows images MUST use manifest version 5 with `boot.kind = firmware`,
`root.format = raw-gpt` and `guest_agents` of `none` or `windows-v1` (the
builder's `guestAgents` argument, `windows-v1` only when the agents are
supplied), with `workspace_source_version` 2 exactly for `windows-v1`. They
MUST NOT be presented as version-4 kernel images, and the Linux
`guest-image-identity` contract in the parent directory MUST NOT be weakened to
admit them.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] windows-editor-runtime-inert
The optional `editorRuntime` staging payload MUST require the Windows v1 agents
and terminal daemon, MUST be copied only to `C:\overalls\editor-runtime`, and
MUST NOT register a listener, worker or task. Its presence MUST preserve the
version-5 windows-v1 manifest without an editor descriptor. The separately
supplied candidate bundle/broker pair MUST use the version-7 windows-editor-v1
contract; native acceptance and separate qualification remain required before
selecting it for fleet browser access.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] windows-editor-candidate-installation
The optional editorBundle/editorBroker candidate MUST require both packages and
the Windows agents with terminald. Its native bundle MUST have an exact source
release descriptor and recursive NAR pin; its fixed independent SYSTEM broker
and worker-custodian tasks MUST each have private scheduler custody, failure
supervision and no execution time limit. Each role MUST use its own checked
trust snapshot so its restart cannot rewrite the other live role's trust input.
Package and authorizer paths MUST prohibit foreign writes and receipt storage MUST be
SYSTEM-only. Every ancestor owner MUST be SYSTEM, Administrators or the exact
Windows TrustedInstaller SID; leaves MUST NOT accept TrustedInstaller ownership.
Candidate installation MUST require at least 2 GiB free writable
headroom, use the separate version-7 windows-editor-v1 manifest with the exact
editor descriptor, and keep package/image qualification metadata false until
native acceptance is recorded. Explicitly combining the pair with windows-v1
MUST refuse. The default v5 and published fleet images MUST NOT acquire either task
from runtime-only staging or select the candidate implicitly.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;network] windows-guest-agents-vsock
Windows guest agents MUST reach Lilly only over virtio-vsock through the pinned
virtio-win `viosock` driver and Winsock provider shipped in the image, speaking
the existing Lilly guest protocols unchanged; the address family MUST be
discovered at runtime, never assumed. The spike probe `overalls-winprobe` MAY
ship only while the real agents do not exist, MUST carry no identity or
credential material and MUST publish only its own log (ADR-0171).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;network] windows-bootstrap-network-from-mmds
A Windows guest MUST learn its placement identity and network only from
Firecracker's MMDS (version 2 session tokens) at boot, through a SYSTEM task
carried in the image: it MUST configure exactly the delivered /32 with an
on-link route to the delivered gateway and a default route through it, route
the private endpoint 169.254.254.1 through the gateway (never on-link), only
the `.internal` namespace to its resolver and every other name to the Linux
guests' public resolvers (1.1.1.1, 9.9.9.9), keep
DHCP and IPv6 disabled, refuse any document whose fields fail validation or
whose MAC is not the adapter's, never log the token or boot challenge, and
grow C: only into space the host added. Nothing about the Administrator
credential, EMS or SAC may change (ADR-0170).


@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] windows-editor-media-archive
An editor candidate ISO MUST stage the native payload as a deterministic regular-file
archive under a short Joliet-safe path with a closed inventory and archive digest.
The SYSTEM installer MUST validate the inventory and regular-file tar listing, reject
traversal, links, duplicate case-insensitive names and stale destinations, extract to
a fresh short staging directory with the fixed Windows tar implementation, verify every
file's size and digest, and only then move the payload to its fixed editor path.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] windows-install-observability
Every Windows installation MUST be observable after the fact without rerunning
it: the build keeps a timestamped timeline of QEMU lifecycle events and guest
serial checkpoints, change-triggered screenshots, the raw serial log, the
driver summary and the Windows Setup and driver-binding logs published by the
guest on its EFI system partition. Guest-side checkpoints MUST be emitted in
every unattend pass that runs code (Windows PE, specialize, SetupComplete) so a
stalled installation can be placed between two known steps.
